{% comment %}
  Clickable LinkedIn preview card: the whole image links to the post.
  Rendered as a block-level <div> so kramdown passes it through verbatim
  (no smart-quotes / escaping). Put a BLANK LINE before this include in posts.
  Usage:
    {% include linkedin_card.liquid img="assets/img/xxx.png" url="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/..." width="220" alt="..." %}
  - img:   path to the screenshot (relative to site root)
  - url:   the LinkedIn post URL to open on click
  - width: max card width in px (optional, defaults to 220)
  - alt:   alt text (optional)
{% endcomment %}
<div class="linkedin-card" style="max-width: {{ include.width | default: 220 }}px; margin: 0.75rem 0;"><a href="{{ include.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="display: block; text-decoration: none;"><img src="{{ include.img | relative_url }}" alt="{{ include.alt | default: 'LinkedIn post' }}" loading="lazy" style="width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06), 0 6px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);" /></a></div>
